425 million dollars. This represents a massive 6,758 million dollar increase over those seven years, reflecting the significant military expansion during World War II.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_6388d2f9e116ac88","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Find Army expenditures for FY 1940 and FY 1947 from treasury bulletins\n- [x] Use reporting structure where Air Force expenditures charged to Army appropriations\n- [ ] Calculate the increase (FY 1947 - FY 1940)\n- [ ] Report answer in millions of dollars to /app/answer.txt\n\nFrom the treasury_bulletin_1948_04_page_13.txt (the older reporting structure where Air Force is included in Army):\n- FY 1940 Army expenditures: 667 million dollars\n- FY 1947 Army expenditures: 7,425 million dollars\n\nIncrease = 7,425 - 667 = 6,758 million dollars"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
